/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.1 Principles and Terminology of Axonometric Projections) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Axonometric projection is a parallel pictorial projection where the object is tilted so) Tj
T*
(that all three principal axes are visible in a single drawing:) Tj
T*
(* Types of Axonometric Projections: Isometric \(all 3 axes equally inclined at 120) Tj
T*
(deg\), Dimetric \(2 axes equally inclined\), Trimetric \(all 3 axes unequally inclined\).) Tj
T*
(* Isometric Axes: Three lines meeting at 120 degrees to each other. In 2D drawing,) Tj
T*
(one axis is vertical, and the other two axes are inclined at 30 degrees to the) Tj
T*
(horizontal.) Tj
T*
(* Isometric Lines: Lines parallel to any of the three isometric axes. Distances along) Tj
T*
(isometric lines can be measured directly to scale.) Tj
T*
(* Non-Isometric Lines: Lines NOT parallel to any isometric axis \(e.g., edges of) Tj
T*
(pyramids, oblique chamfers\). Cannot be measured directly; must be located via) Tj
T*
(coordinates of their endpoints.) Tj
T*
(* Isometric Planes \(Isoplanes\): Three coordinate planes defined by pairs of isometric) Tj
T*
(axes: Isoplane Left \(30 deg left & vertical\), Isoplane Right \(30 deg right &) Tj
T*
(vertical\), Isoplane Top \(30 deg left & 30 deg right\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.2 Isometric Projection vs Isometric View) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Isometric Projection: Drawn using foreshortened Isometric Scale. Length = True) Tj
T*
(Length x cos\(45\) / cos\(30\) = sqrt\(2\)/sqrt\(3\) approx 0.816 \(81.6% of True Length\).) Tj
T*
(* Isometric View \(or Isometric Drawing\): Drawn using True Scale \(100% full scale) Tj
T*
(dimensions\). The drawing is identical in proportion to isometric projection but is) Tj
T*
(approximately 22.5% larger in visual area.) Tj
T*
(* Isometric Scale Construction: Draw horizontal line. From origin, draw line at 30) Tj
T*
(degrees \(Isometric scale\) and line at 45 degrees \(True scale\). Project true divisions) Tj
T*
(vertically down onto the 30-degree line.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.3 Methods of Drawing Isometric Projections) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
