T*
(* 1. Box Method: Enclose the entire object inside an imaginary isometric rectangular) Tj
T*
(box of length L, width W, and height H. Carve out features by measuring along) Tj
T*
(isometric box edges. Essential for irregular objects, prisms, pyramids.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Coordinate / Offset Method: Locate individual key corner vertices in space using) Tj
T*
(X, Y, Z coordinates measured from a defined reference corner.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Four-Center Method for Isometric Circles \(Ellipses\): A circle in orthographic) Tj
T*
(view appears as an ellipse in isometric view. Inscribed in an isometric rhombus) Tj
T*
(\(rhombus side = circle diameter\). Drawn using four arcs struck from the two obtuse) Tj
T*
(angle vertices and the intersections of opposite side perpendicular bisectors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.4 AutoCAD 3D Modeling Fundamentals) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* 3D Coordinate Systems: World Coordinate System \(WCS\) is fixed. User Coordinate) Tj
T*
(System \(UCS\) can be dynamically rotated and translated to align with any 3D face) Tj
T*
(using UCS -> 3Point \(Origin, X-axis, Y-axis\).) Tj
T*
(* 3D Primitive Solids: BOX, CYLINDER, CONE, SPHERE, TORUS, WEDGE, PYRAMID.) Tj
T*
(* 3D Solid Generation Commands:) Tj
T*
(- EXTRUDE \(EXT\): Projects an enclosed planar 2D curve or region along a perpendicular) Tj
T*
(height or specified path.) Tj
T*
(- REVOLVE \(REV\): Rotates a planar 2D profile around a specified axis of revolution by up) Tj
T*
(to 360 degrees.) Tj
T*
(- PRESSPULL: Dynamically extrudes an enclosed boundary area or face directly without) Tj
T*
(needing a prior Region entity.) Tj
T*
(- SWEEP & LOFT: Generates solids along arbitrary 3D guide curves or between multiple) Tj
T*
(distinct cross-sectional profiles.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
