([PROBLEM 1: Isometric View of a Hexagonal Prism using Box Method]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: A hexagonal prism has base side 30 mm and axis height 65 mm. The) Tj
T*
(prism rests with its base on HP with one base edge parallel to VP. Draw its Isometric) Tj
T*
(View.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
(* Step 1: Orthographic Base & Enclosing Box:) Tj
T*
(- Draw a regular hexagon of side 30 mm in orthographic plan view.) Tj
T*
(- Enclose the hexagon in a tight rectangle ABCD. Length L = distance across corners = 2) Tj
T*
(x 30 = 60 mm. Width W = distance across flats = 2 x 30 x cos\(30\) = 51.96 mm.) Tj
T*
(* Step 2: Isometric Enclosing Box:) Tj
T*
(- Draw isometric axes \(one vertical, two at 30 deg to horizontal\).) Tj
T*
ET

