([PROBLEM 2: Four-Center Method Construction of Isometric Cylinder]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Draw the Isometric View of a vertical right circular cylinder of base) Tj
T*
(diameter 50 mm and height 70 mm.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Four-Center Method Execution:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Top Face Rhombus: Draw isometric rhombus ABCD of side 50 mm on Isoplane Top) Tj
T*
(\(axes at 30 deg to left and 30 deg to right\). Obtuse angle vertices are at B \(top\)) Tj
T*
(and D \(bottom\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Finding Centers:) Tj
T*
(- Find midpoints 1, 2, 3, 4 of rhombus sides AB, BC, CD, DA.) Tj
T*
(- From obtuse vertex B, draw lines to opposite midpoints 3 and 4.) Tj
T*
(- From obtuse vertex D, draw lines to opposite midpoints 1 and 2.) Tj
T*
(- The intersections of these lines establish two sharp centers C1 and C2.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Striking Ellipse Arcs:) Tj
T*
(- Center B, radius B-3: Draw large arc 3-4.) Tj
T*
(- Center D, radius D-1: Draw large arc 1-2.) Tj
T*
(- Center C1, radius C1-1: Draw small arc 1-4.) Tj
T*
(- Center C2, radius C2-2: Draw small arc 2-3. \(Completes smooth 4-arc top ellipse\).) Tj
T*
(* 4. Bottom Base Ellipse: Project centers B, D, C1, C2 vertically downward by 70 mm.) Tj
T*
(Strike identical lower arcs for the front half 1-2-3.) Tj
T*
(* 5. Tangent Generators: Draw two vertical lines tangent to the outer extremities of) Tj
T*
(the top and bottom ellipses. Erase construction guides.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
