(Problem Statement: A solid sphere of diameter 40 mm rests centrally on the top face of a) Tj
T*
(cubical block of side 60 mm. Draw the Isometric Projection of the composite assembly.) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation & Construction Protocol:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Cube Construction \(Isometric Scale\): Side of cube in isometric projection = 60) Tj
T*
(mm x 0.816 = 48.96 mm. Draw isometric box of side 49 mm.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Locate Center of Sphere:) Tj
T*
(- Find center of top face of cube by intersecting diagonal lines.) Tj
T*
(- The geometric center of the sphere lies vertically above the top face at a distance) Tj
T*
(equal to the sphere radius.) Tj
T*
(- Isometric height of center = 20 mm x 0.816 = 16.32 mm above the cube face. Mark sphere) Tj
T*
(center point O.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Sphere Outline in Isometric Projection:) Tj
T*
(- CRITICAL RULE: In axonometric / isometric projection, a sphere always projects as a) Tj
T*
(TRUE CIRCLE! It does NOT become an ellipse.) Tj
T*
(- Radius of circle in projection = TRUE radius of sphere = 20.0 mm \(NOT foreshortened,) Tj
T*
(because the sphere contour in all directions remains perpendicular to sight rays\).) Tj
T*
(- Center at point O, draw a true circle of radius 20 mm.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Visible Outlines: Top face of cube partially hidden beneath sphere silhouette;) Tj
T*
(finish visible edges with solid thick lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
