([PROBLEM 4: AutoCAD 3D Solid Modeling Sequence for Stepped Flange]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Model a 3D stepped shaft with circular flange and counterbored hole) Tj
T*
(using AutoCAD 3D tools.) Tj
T*
(AutoCAD Command Protocol:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Workspace: Switch to "3D Modeling" workspace. Set Visual Style to "Shaded with) Tj
T*
(edges".) Tj
T*
(* 2. REVOLVE Method:) Tj
T*
(- Draw 2D half-cross-sectional profile using PLINE: Start at 0,0 -> 15,0 -> 15,60 ->) Tj
T*
(45,60 -> 45,80 -> 0,80 -> Close.) Tj
T*
(- REVOLVE -> Select polyline -> Axis of revolution: 0,0 to 0,80 -> Angle: 360 deg.) Tj
T*
(\(Generates stepped solid cylinder\).) Tj
T*
(* 3. CYLINDER for Central Bore:) Tj
T*
(- CYLINDER -> Center: 0,0,0 -> Radius: 15 mm -> Height: 80 mm.) Tj
T*
(* 4. SUBTRACT Command:) Tj
T*
(- SUBTRACT -> Select outer stepped solid -> Press Enter -> Select inner cylinder ->) Tj
T*
(Press Enter. \(Produces hollow through bore\).) Tj
T*
(* 5. 3P UCS for Flange Bolt Holes:) Tj
T*
(- UCS -> 3P -> Click flange center, X-axis, Y-axis.) Tj
T*
(- CYLINDER -> Center: 30,0,60 -> Radius: 4 mm -> Height: -20 mm.) Tj
T*
ET

